<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<qti-assessment-item xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0 https://purl.imsglobal.org/spec/qti/v3p0/schema/xsd/imsqti_asiv3p0_v1p0.xsd"
  identifier="sat-c1-u01-archaic-pilot-s4-q3" title="4 Apply -- question 3" adaptive="true" time-dependent="false">

  <qti-response-declaration identifier="RESPONSE" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-correct-response><qti-value>D</qti-value></qti-correct-response>
  </qti-response-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="SCORE" cardinality="single" base-type="float">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>0</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="FEEDBACK" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier"/>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="C_BACK" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>off</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>

  <qti-item-body>

        <p>Tracing her family's farm across an 1843 county map, Elena kept stumbling over villages she could not find in any modern atlas.</p>
        <p>The settlements still existed; only their names had moved on.</p>
        <p>The map's labels were archaic, recording what each place was called before the railway companies renamed whole districts to suit their timetables.</p>
        <p>Locals had not spoken the old names in four generations, and the road signs Elena passed that afternoon bore no trace of them.</p>
        <p>Only in the parish registers, and on maps like hers, did the older names survive at all.</p>
        <p>In which of these sentences is archaic used correctly?</p>
        <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="true" max-choices="1">
          <qti-simple-choice identifier="A">Her archaic outfit looked very modern and fashionable.</qti-simple-choice>
          <qti-simple-choice identifier="B">The recipe was too archaic even though it's made daily.</qti-simple-choice>
          <qti-simple-choice identifier="C">That archaic dance is performed at every school event.</qti-simple-choice>
          <qti-simple-choice identifier="D">The historian discovered archaic texts from the fifth century.</qti-simple-choice>
        </qti-choice-interaction>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-A" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>This contradicts itself: archaic means belonging to an earlier era and no longer in use, so an archaic outfit can't look 'very modern and fashionable' — modern is the word's direct opposite.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-B" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>A recipe that's made daily is still in current use. Archaic means old and no longer used — the 'even though it's made daily' clause is exactly what rules the word out.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-C" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>A dance performed at every school event is still in active use today. Archaic specifically means out of use — not merely old — so it doesn't fit something performed all the time.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-D" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Correct. Texts from the fifth century belong to an earlier period, written in language that has long since fallen out of use — old and no longer current is exactly what archaic means.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="on" outcome-identifier="C_BACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body>
        <h4>Word Choice</h4>
        <p><em>formal / literary</em></p>
        <p>Archaic is a scholarly word for things that belong to a vanished past. In everyday speech, say 'old-fashioned' or 'outdated.' Reach for archaic when describing vocabulary, customs, or styles that clearly belong to a historical era.</p>
      </qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
  </qti-item-body>

  <qti-response-processing>
    <qti-response-condition>
      <qti-response-if>
        <qti-match><qti-variable identifier="RESPONSE"/><qti-correct identifier="RESPONSE"/></qti-match>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="SCORE"><qti-base-value base-type="float">1</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="completionStatus"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">completed</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="FEEDBACK"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">correct</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="C_BACK"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">on</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
      </qti-response-if>
      <qti-response-else>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="SCORE"><qti-base-value base-type="float">0</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="completionStatus"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">incomplete</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="FEEDBACK"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">incorrect</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
      </qti-response-else>
    </qti-response-condition>
    <qti-response-condition>
      <qti-response-if>
        <qti-match><qti-variable identifier="RESPONSE"/><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">A</qti-base-value></qti-match>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="FEEDBACK"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">FB-A</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
      </qti-response-if>
    </qti-response-condition>
    <qti-response-condition>
      <qti-response-if>
        <qti-match><qti-variable identifier="RESPONSE"/><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">B</qti-base-value></qti-match>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="FEEDBACK"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">FB-B</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
      </qti-response-if>
    </qti-response-condition>
    <qti-response-condition>
      <qti-response-if>
        <qti-match><qti-variable identifier="RESPONSE"/><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">C</qti-base-value></qti-match>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="FEEDBACK"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">FB-C</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
      </qti-response-if>
    </qti-response-condition>
  </qti-response-processing>
</qti-assessment-item>
